{% doc %}
  The collector card, at the top of the media column on the Tee of the Week.

  @param {object} product - The tee. The caller decides whether to show it; this
    snippet does not re-test, because the block needs the same answer to collapse
    the gallery and Liquid cannot read a variable back out of a render.

  IT IS THE LIVE SLAB, NOT A PICTURE OF ONE. This showed the PNG that
  `enrich.tee_card_url` points at — the image the app renders for ad creative —
  and it was a flat sticker next to a homepage card that leans, straightens under
  the cursor and catches the light. Same card, two experiences, and the PDP got
  the lesser one. It now renders `aj-tee-slab`, the same snippet the homepage
  section uses, so there is one card and it behaves the same everywhere.

  THAT ALSO CLOSED A SEAM. The old gate needed the metafield to be populated, and
  nothing wrote it on rotation — it was set by hand for week 001. Every following
  week would have shown a bare gallery with no error anywhere. The test is now
  the same one `aj-deal-eyebrow` uses, so the eyebrow and the card cannot
  disagree about which product is this week's tee, and neither needs maintenance.

  The PNG is still rendered and still used — by the ads, which need a flat image.
  It is simply no longer what the product page shows.

  WHY IT IS NOT THE PRODUCT IMAGE, which is the more obvious way to do all this.
  Adding the card to the product's media would push it into the Google and Meta
  feeds, and Merchant Center prohibits promotional overlays on product images.
  The card has a struck price and a discount roundel on it, so that route would
  inject a policy violation into the feed of an account already suspended once
  for misrepresentation. So it renders here, on the page, and never enters the
  catalogue.
{% enddoc %}

<div class="aj-teecard">
  {% render 'aj-tee-slab', tee: product, standalone: true, linked: false %}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    The slab sizes itself — 22rem capped and centred, the same as the homepage.
    All this wrapper does is hold it off the disclosure below.
  */
  .aj-teecard {
    margin-block-end: var(--padding-md, 1rem);
  }

  /* ---- the disclosure holding the supplier photographs ------------------- */

  .aj-teecard__more {
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
  }

  /*
    Same purple uppercase label as the mega menu, the category drill-down and
    the footer contact block. A control that looks like every other label on the
    site does not need explaining.
  */
  .aj-teecard__more-label {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    padding-block: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* Safari still paints its own triangle without this. */
  .aj-teecard__more-label::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .aj-teecard__more-label::after {
    content: "";
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    border-right: 2px solid currentcolor;
    border-bottom: 2px solid currentcolor;
    transform: rotate(45deg) translate(-0.1em, -0.1em);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }

  .aj-teecard__more[open] .aj-teecard__more-label::after {
    transform: rotate(-135deg) translate(-0.15em, -0.15em);
  }

  .aj-teecard__more-label:hover {
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
  }

  /* One label, two states, no JavaScript. */
  .aj-teecard__more [data-when-open] {
    display: none;
  }

  .aj-teecard__more[open] [data-when-open] {
    display: inline;
  }

  .aj-teecard__more[open] [data-when-closed] {
    display: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
